  "translationRepairs": [
    ["s0027","idiomatic","The doctors under the Grand Secretariat of Rites determined that the four deputy music supervisors, two music masters, two torchbearers, and two score keepers should all wear purple gauze official robes, black gauze futou with spread corners, red leather horn belts, wooden tablets, and black boots.","The doctors under the Court of Imperial Sacrifices determined that the four deputy music supervisors, two music masters, two torchbearers, and two score keepers should all wear purple gauze official robes, black gauze futou with spread corners, red leather horn belts, wooden tablets, and black boots.","s0027 opens with 太常寺下博士議定; 太常寺 is the Court of Imperial Sacrifices, not the Grand Secretariat. The proposed idiomatic correctly renames the office while leaving the costume list intact.","high","applied"],
    ["s0027","literal","The doctors under the Grand Secretariat of Rites deliberated and fixed: four deputy music supervisors, two music masters, two torchbearers, and two score keepers—all wear purple gauze official robes, black gauze futou with spread corners, red leather horn belts, wooden tablets, and black boots.","The doctors under the Court of Imperial Sacrifices deliberated and fixed: four deputy music supervisors, two music masters, two torchbearers, and two score keepers—all wear purple gauze official robes, black gauze futou with spread corners, red leather horn belts, wooden tablets, and black boots.","The literal likewise misrenders 太常寺 as Grand Secretariat of Rites. Court of Imperial Sacrifices is the accurate institutional reading for this unit.","high","applied"],
    ["s0031","idiomatic","(In Zhang Zhen's 《Successive Ages as Models》, archivist of the Jin Grand Secretariat of Rites, Jin dancers wore black four-layered jackets with yellow mouth-pieces hanging at the sides and yellow gauze forehead bands. The jackets were silk, bearing colored plaques on chest and back, on each shoulder, and joining front and back, all embroidered with paired luan in coiling flight and sewn to the garment.","(In Zhang Zhen's 《Successive Ages as Models》, archivist of the Jin Court of Imperial Sacrifices, Jin dancers wore black four-layered jackets with yellow mouth-pieces hanging at the sides and yellow gauze forehead bands. The jackets were silk, bearing colored plaques on chest and back, on each shoulder, and joining front and back, all embroidered with paired luan in coiling flight and sewn to the garment.","s0031 has 金太常寺掌故張珍; 太常寺 is the Court of Imperial Sacrifices under Jin, not a Grand Secretariat. The proposed idiomatic correctly restores Zhang Zhen's office title.","high","applied"],
    ["s0031","literal","(Zhang Zhen, archivist of the Jin Grand Secretariat of Rites, records Jin practice in his 《Successive Ages as Models》: dancers wore black jackets, all four-layered, with yellow mouth-pieces hanging to left and right, and yellow gauze forehead bands; the jackets were of silk, with two plaques on chest and back, two on each shoulder, and one joining front and back—all in colors, embroidered with paired luan in coiling flight, sewn onto the jacket.","(Zhang Zhen, archivist of the Jin Court of Imperial Sacrifices, records Jin practice in his 《Successive Ages as Models》: dancers wore black jackets, all four-layered, with yellow mouth-pieces hanging to left and right, and yellow gauze forehead bands; the jackets were of silk, with two plaques on chest and back, two on each shoulder, and one joining front and back—all in colors, embroidered with paired luan in coiling flight, sewn onto the jacket.","The literal repeats the same misreading of 金太常寺 as Grand Secretariat of Rites. Court of Imperial Sacrifices matches the Chinese office name.","high","applied"],
    ["s0037","idiomatic","In the seventh month the Secretariat's Ministry of Personnel again ratified the Grand Secretariat doctors' decision and ordered the responsible offices to manufacture the garments.","In the seventh month the Secretariat's Ministry of Personnel again ratified the Court of Imperial Sacrifices doctors' decision and ordered the responsible offices to manufacture the garments.","s0037 has 中書吏部再準太常博士議定; 太常博士 are doctors of the Court of Imperial Sacrifices. The proposed idiomatic correctly attributes the decision while preserving 中書吏部 as the Secretariat's Ministry of Personnel.","high","applied"],
    ["s0037","literal","In the seventh month, the Secretariat's Ministry of Personnel again approved the doctors' deliberation of the Grand Secretariat of Rites and ordered the responsible offices to manufacture them.","In the seventh month, the Secretariat's Ministry of Personnel again approved the doctors' deliberation of the Court of Imperial Sacrifices and ordered the responsible offices to manufacture them.","The literal likewise assigns 太常博士 to a Grand Secretariat of Rites. Court of Imperial Sacrifices is the correct institutional affiliation of those doctors.","high","applied"],
    ["s0278","idiomatic","Next came sixteen musicians in Five Blessings crowns and brocade robes, with six dragon flutes, six suona, and four zhanggu, joining the preceding Great Music in 《Gold-Letter Western Barbarian Sutra》.","Next came sixteen musicians in Five Blessings crowns and brocade robes, with six dragon flutes, six bili, and four zhanggu, joining the preceding Great Music in 《Gold-Letter Western Barbarian Sutra》.","s0278 lists 觱栗六 among the instruments; 觱栗/觱篥 is the bili double-reed pipe, not the suona (嗩吶). The proposed idiomatic correctly names the instrument.","high","applied"],
    ["s0278","literal","Next, the seventh formation: sixteen musicians wearing Five Blessings crowns, brocade robes; six dragon flutes, six suona, four zhanggu; together with the preceding Great Music they played 《Gold-Letter Western Barbarian Sutra》.","Next, the seventh formation: sixteen musicians wearing Five Blessings crowns, brocade robes; six dragon flutes, six bili, four zhanggu; together with the preceding Great Music they played 《Gold-Letter Western Barbarian Sutra》.","The literal likewise mistranslates 觱栗 as suona. Bili is the accurate instrument name for this count of six.","high","applied"]
  ],
